(7463336, 1183768, 103142, '<td valign="top">I like the shot quite a bit. I like the unconventional crop with no head space in front and a lot behind. It gives it a little more tension -- which made me think she''s run out of money for paying. Just the moment before challenge and the way you''ve shot it made my imagination start running. :) -8- for the jog</td>', 'I like the shot quite a bit. I like the unconventional crop with no head space in front and a lot behind. It gives it a little more tension -- which made me think she''s run out of money for paying. Just the moment before challenge and the way you''ve shot it made my imagination start running. :) -8- for the jog', '2016-07-07 11:29:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7463337, 1183614, 103142, '<td valign="top">Holy Crap! what a great catch! I want to see his picture, too! <br/> <br/>One of those photos that isn''t eye candy pretty, but where you need to sit and realize what you''re seeing. Makes me wonder what it would look like in b&amp;w. I''m having fun looking at this and having multiple thoughts run through my head. For instance, the head taking up so much of the frame, it makes the elephant look smaller and not as menacing. Would cropping make it better? I don''t think so. Couldn''t have used a longer lens. B&amp;W? But the dust color is too wonderful. Just need it blown up and bigger? That helped. <br/> <br/>Thanks for the photo and the adventure in thought processing. :) -8-</td>', 'Holy Crap! what a great catch! I want to see his picture, too!  One of those photos that isn''t eye candy pretty, but where you need to sit and realize what you''re seeing. Makes me wonder what it would look like in b&w. I''m having fun looking at this and having multiple thoughts run through my head. For instance, the head taking up so much of the frame, it makes the elephant look smaller and not as menacing. Would cropping make it better? I don''t think so. Couldn''t have used a longer lens. B&W? But the dust color is too wonderful. Just need it blown up and bigger? That helped.  Thanks for the photo and the adventure in thought processing. :) -8-', '2016-07-07 11:29:34.000000', NULL, 1),
